{"parseRefreshTokenResponse injects a placeholder 'refresh_token' string when missing, and Office365/Zoom persist this value, which can overwrite the real refresh token and break future refresh attempts": 0.9375792741775513, "minimumTokenResponseSchema uses computed keys like [z.string().toString()] inside z.object, creating literal property names rather than accepting arbitrary expiry fields, so parseRefreshTokenResponse will reject typical token payloads": 0.9252592921257019, "GoogleCalendarService stores the Zod safeParse result object (containing {success, data}) into credential.key instead of the actual credential data, corrupting the credential JSON so future googleCredentialSchema.parse calls will fail": 0.9820178747177124, "refreshOAuthTokens returns a fetch Response when syncing is enabled, but several integrations (Hubspot, Zoho) expect an Axios response or provider token object and access .data/.expiresIn fields, causing runtime failures during token refresh": 0.9497768878936768, "SalesforceCalendarService calls prisma.credential.update but never imports prisma, causing a ReferenceError/build failure": 0.8028537034988403, "SalesforceCalendarService refreshes and stores a new access token but still constructs the jsforce.Connection using the old credentialKey.access_token, negating the refresh for in-memory usage": 0.894907534122467, "Webhook handler uses zod.parse, symmetricDecrypt, and JSON.parse without try/catch or defaultHandler, so malformed bodies or decrypt/JSON errors will return 500s instead of controlled 4xx responses": 0.967557430267334}